WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.760
Chocolate has been long
maligned when it comes to acne.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.200
But is it the cocoa itself
or the sugar and dairy

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.600
that come with it
that causes acne?

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.898
Watch to find out.

00:00:11.898 --> 00:00:18.248
"Do Chocolate and Cocoa
Powder Cause Acne?"

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.400
Acne affects nearly 1 in
10 people in the world,

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.480
making it perhaps the eighth
most prevalent disease worldwide.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.840
What’s the role of nutrition?

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.040
Well, go back a century
and dermatology textbooks

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.160
were recommending various
dietary restrictions.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.160
For example, recommending
those with acne

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.640
avoid foods like pork, sausage, cheese,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.840
pickles, pastries, sweets,
cocoa, and chocolate.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.720
Yeah, but old-timey medicine
was full of crackpot theories.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.800
Dr. Kellogg, for example,
blamed acne on masturbation.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.000
Nothing a few corn flakes
couldn’t fix though...

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.360
Population studies have
found associations

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.440
between acne and the
consumption of foods

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.520
like dairy, sweets, and chocolate,

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.360
but you don’t know if
it’s cause and effect...

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.080
until you put it to the test.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.760
There have been high quality reports,
like the Harvard Nurse’s study,

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.880
that looked at nearly 50,000 women

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.800
and found a link between adolescent
milk drinking and acne,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.560
particularly skim milk,

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:25.920
something that’s been found
for teenage boys as well.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.880
They thought it might be the hormones
in milk that were responsible,

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.760
but it could also be
the milk protein, whey,

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:33.440
of which they add
extra to skim milk

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:36.480
to make it less watery,
which may play a role directly

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.080
in acne formation or
as hormonal carriers.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.400
That would explain
cases like this:

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.920
where whey protein
powders were implicated

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.560
in precipitating acne
flares in teens

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.320
who had acne that just didn’t
seem to want to go away

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.720
until they stopped the whey.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.760
It doesn’t appear to just
be a protein effect,

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.720
since soy protein
supplements, for example,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.960
did not seem to cause
the same problem.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.480
But, for dairy, in terms
of interventional studies,

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.360
all we have are these
kinds of case series.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.400
If you do a systematic review
of acne and nutrition,

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.720
you get results like this for dairy:

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.400
out of the 20 or so papers
on acne and dairy out there,

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.120
about three-quarters
suggest adverse effects,

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.960
and the remainder
report no effect,

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.080
with no studies suggesting
a beneficial effect

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:26.960
of dairy on acne;

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:29.040
so, you could look at
this and conclude

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.200
a dairy-free diet is worth a try.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.640
But, this is based
on low-grade evidence,

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:36.080
level C and D evidence,

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.080
where C is like the
population studies,

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:41.360
and D is kind of like those
series of case reports.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.600
What we want ideally
are randomized

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.560
interventional studies,
level A and B evidence,

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:52.000
which we don’t have for dairy,
but we do have for chocolate.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.080
When it comes to acne,

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.920
no food is more universally
condemned than chocolate.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.280
So, if you’re the Chocolate
Manufacturers Association,

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.600
how are you going
to design a study

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.000
to make your product
not look so bad?

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.840
Well, you can always use
the old drug company trick

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.960
of pitting your product against
something even worse;

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.080
and so, they fed people

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.800
chocolate bars versus
fake chocolate bars

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.080
made out of a partially
hydrogenated vegetable oil:

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.040
trans fats.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.960
So, make it have more sugar,
throw in some milk protein,

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.600
and make it 28% pure trans fat laden,
Crisco-like vegetable shortening.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:33.440
And surprise, surprise
there were just as many pimples

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.200
on the fake chocolate bars,

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.400
allowing them to conclude
that eating high amounts

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:43.120
of chocolate is A-OK
when it comes to acne.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.240
And, the medical community fell for it.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:50.080
“Have we been guilty of
taking candy away from babies?”

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.320
“Too many patients harbor the delusion

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.360
that their health can somehow
be mysteriously harmed

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.800
by something in their diet.”

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.560
That original study “finding
that chocolate consumption

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:03.280
supposedly does not
exacerbate acne

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.920
has continued to remain
virtually unchallenged

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:10.160
for decades and continues to be cited”
even in recent reviews.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.200
For example, this pediatrics journal.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.480
Years ago, it was demonstrated

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.440
that chocolate consumption
had no effect on acne.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:20.320
“This serves as a
cautionary example

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.400
of how ‘research-
based evidence’

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.400
should be vigorously scrutinized

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:27.520
prior to being incorporated
into clinical practice.”

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.360
Just because something
is published in the

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.200
Journal of the American
Medical Association

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.560
doesn’t necessarily mean
it’s a good study,

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.000
especially when industry
interests are involved.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.200
Maybe we should be
telling acne patients

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.920
to try cutting down on not
only the sweets and the dairy

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.040
but also the trans fats

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.440
found in partially hydrogenated
vegetable oils,

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:52.560
but we can’t be unequivocal
in our advice to acne sufferers

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.360
on foods to include
or exclude until...

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:59.040
they’re put to the test
in well-designed randomized

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.560
controlled clinical trials.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:05.360
But there simply weren’t any
such trials on acne, until...

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:09.840
Now, which we’ll cover, next.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.960
A century ago, diet was commonly used
as part of the treatment for acne.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:21.040
During the 1960s, however,
the diet–acne connection

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:21.840
fell out of favor.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:22.900
Why?

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:26.000
Because of a study
purported to “prove”

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.480
that chocolate had no
influence on acne

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.920
by comparing a chocolate bar
to a pseudo-chocolate bar

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:34.480
composed of 28% pure trans fat

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.720
laden partially hydrogenated
vegetable oil,

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:40.960
a substance known to
increase signs of inflammation.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.480
Compared to that, no wonder

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.200
that chocolate didn’t come
out looking so bad.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.800
And then, there was
this other study

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:50.240
where small groups of
medical students

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.160
ate a variety of
purported culprits

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:54.080
and only about a
third broke out,

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.920
but there was no control
group to compare to,

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:01.760
yet these two studies, despite
their “major design flaws,

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:05.200
were sufficient to
dissociate diet from acne

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:07.360
in the minds of
most dermatologists.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.440
Textbooks were revised
to reflect

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.520
this new academic consensus,

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:13.120
and dermatologists
took the stance

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.960
that any mumblings about
the association

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:17.600
between diet and acne
were unscientific

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:21.200
and one of the many myths
surrounding this ubiquitous disease.”

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.080
Comments such as,
“The association of diet

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:27.920
with acne has been relegated
to the category of myth”

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.520
are commonplace in
both the past

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.040
and current medical literature,

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.880
yet the major dermatology
textbooks promulgating this notion

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.280
that diet and acne
are unrelated,

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:40.480
rely only on those
two flawed studies.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:44.240
So, this current thought
within the dermatology community

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.320
that diet and acne
are unrelated

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:49.680
has little or no
factual support.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.840
And, there’s reason to suspect

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.720
chocolate consumption
may be an issue.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.880
If you take blood from people
before and after eating

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:59.040
a couple of bars
of milk chocolate,

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:02.160
it appears to prime
some of your pus cells

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:04.080
to release extra
inflammatory chemicals,

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.840
when you expose them
to acne-causing

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.600
bacteria in a petri dish.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:10.800
So, maybe this is
one of the mechanisms

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:12.960
that could explain the effects
of chocolate on acne,

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:16.160
but how do we know
it’s the chocolate

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:17.920
and not the added
sugar or milk?

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:20.560
Yes, if you survey teens

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.720
on their acne severity
and eating habits,

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:25.360
there appears to be a link
to chocolate consumption,

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:28.800
but is that people sprinkling
cocoa powder in their smoothies,

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.880
or eating dark chocolate or,

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:32.960
is it because of the
added sugar and milk?

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:34.560
Just cutting down
on sugary foods

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:37.760
and refined grains
can cut pimple counts

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:39.280
in half in a few months,

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:42.000
significantly better
than the control group,

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:45.440
complete with compelling
before and after pictures.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.760
To tease out if
it was the sugar,

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.680
researchers gave
people milk chocolate

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:51.600
versus jelly beans.

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:55.040
If it was just the sugar,
then acne would presumably

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:59.440
get equally worse in both groups,
but instead, the chocolate group

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:01.680
got worse—a doubling
of acne lesions,

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.840
whereas no change in
the jelly bean group.

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:06.800
So, it’s apparently
not just the sugar,

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.080
maybe there is something
in chocolate,

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:13.040
or is it only in
milk chocolate?

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:15.200
So far, there have
been no studies

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:19.040
assessing the effects of pure
100% chocolate on acne,

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.480
that is, until...

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.240
there were!

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:24.320
57 volunteers with
mild-to-moderate acne

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:25.840
were randomized into three groups,

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.000
receiving white
chocolate bars,

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.160
dark chocolate bars,
or no chocolate bars

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.440
every day for a month.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.120
And, this wasn’t
just dark chocolate,

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:34.800
but 100% chocolate,

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.400
meaning like
baker’s chocolate.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:38.800
Unlike pure dark chocolate,
white chocolate is packed

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:39.760
with sugar and milk.

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:42.000
And, indeed,
acne lesions worsened

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:42.960
in the white
chocolate group,

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.680
but not in the dark
chocolate or control groups.

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:47.680
So, in this study,
white, but not dark,

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.760
chocolate consumption
was associated

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:52.240
with an exacerbation
of acne lesions.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:56.720
But, other studies did show acne
worsening on dark chocolate.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:59.040
Give research subjects
a single big load

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:04.160
of Ghirardelli baking chocolate,
and they broke out within days.

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.480
A significant increase
in the total average number

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.280
of acne lesions
within 4 days.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.240
And, same thing
with more chronic

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:13.840
dark chocolate consumption:

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:16.400
a half a small chocolate
bar a day for a month,

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:20.640
and increased acne severity
was reported within 2 weeks,

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:23.520
with before-and-after
pictures looking like this.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:27.840
OK, but what was lacking
in these two studies?

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:30.960
Give people chocolate every day
and their acne gets worse,

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.680
or one big load of chocolate
and their acne gets worse.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.480
What didn’t these
studies include?

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:40.560
Long-time NutritionFacts followers
should know this by now.

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:44.080
Right, they’re missing
a control group.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:46.000
If you look at surveys,

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.840
most people believe
chocolate causes acne;

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:50.000
so, if you give people a
big load of chocolate,

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.320
maybe just the stress
and expectation

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.680
that they’re going
to have an outbreak

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:55.920
contributes to the
actual outbreak.

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:57.680
To really get to
the bottom of this,

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.520
you’d have to
design a study

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:01.600
where you give people
disguised chocolate.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:04.320
You expose people to chocolate
without them knowing it

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:06.080
and see if they
still break out.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:08.400
Like you could
put cocoa powder

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:11.040
into opaque capsules,
so they don’t know

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.880
if they’re getting
cocoa or placebo,

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.480
and that would have
the additional benefit

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.040
of eliminating the cocoa
butter fat factor.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.640
No milk, no sugar, no fat,

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:21.360
just pure cocoa powder in
capsules versus placebo,

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:25.520
but there's never been
such a study until...

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:26.900
Now.

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:30.560
A double-blind, placebo-controlled
study assessing the effects of

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:33.760
chocolate consumption,
actually cocoa powder consumption,

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:36.720
in subjects with
a history of acne –

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.000
assigned to swallow capsules

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:40.320
filled with either
unsweetened 100% cocoa,

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:43.520
or a placebo of like an unflavored,
unsweetened jello powder.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:47.760
Just a one-time binge
requiring the swallowing

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:50.480
of up to 240 capsules to try to

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:52.640
secretly expose people
to a few ounces

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:57.760
of cocoa powder and…
the same significant increase,

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:59.760
the same doubling
of acne lesions

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:00.560
within 4 days,

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:01.920
like in the Ghirardelli study.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:04.720
So, sadly, it
really does appear

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.640
that in acne-prone individuals,

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:10.320
the consumption of cocoa
may cause an increase in acne.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:13.360
Now, the study did
just include men;

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.960
so, they didn’t have to deal

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:17.120
with cyclical
hormonal changes,

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:19.600
and it’s hard to imagine
that the real cocoa group,

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:21.600
after swallowing
hundreds of capsules,

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:23.760
didn’t burp up some cocoa taste

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.400
and know they were not
just in the placebo group.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.280
But, the best available
balance of evidence

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:31.760
does suggest that if
you’re bothered by acne,

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:34.720
you may want to try backing off
on chocolate to see

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:37.817
if your symptoms improve.

